    "object": {
      "Graph": {
        "@Type": "f8a58466",
        "@Value": {
          "Implementation": {
            "@Type": "3b83b776",
            "@Value": {
              "TextDocument": {
                "@Type": "f3878285",
                "@Value": {
                  "TextBlobForSerialisation": "(string)IF find(head, cell) THEN\n\tcdr := cell.cdr;\nELSE\n\tcdr := CONS_NIL;\nEND_IF\n",
                  "LineInfoPersistence": "(string)fcfe7f67-243d-48af-854c-5b0df9b9c3a3_Impl_LineIds"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "Interface": {
            "@Type": "a9ed5b7e",
            "@Value": {
              "TextDocument": {
                "@Type": "f3878285",
                "@Value": {
                  "TextBlobForSerialisation": "(string)(*\n================================================================================\nFunction Block Method : ConsHeap.cdr\n\nPurpose:\n    Reads the cdr value of a cons cell.\n\nApplication:\n    Call to read the next register linked from a list cell.\n\nOperation:\n    1. Looks up the cell identified by head.\n    2. Returns the cell's cdr when the register is valid.\n\nInputs:\n    head - Register of the cell to read.\n\nOutputs:\n    None.\n\nInOut:\n    None.\n\nReturn Value:\n    CONS_REG - Cell cdr value, or CONS_NIL when head has no tail.\n\nAssumptions:\n    - head identifies a cell in this heap.\n\nLimitations:\n    - An invalid register returns CONS_NIL, the same value used for an\n      empty list. This is a fail-safe behaviour but may not distinguish\n      between an empty list and an invalid register. In effect, every\n      invalid register exists but always treated as having no tail.\n\nDependencies:\n    - ConsHeap.find.\n    - CONS_NIL.\n\nExample:\n\n    tail := fbConsHeap.cdr(head := tail);\n\nRevision History:\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Date         Version  Author           Description\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    13/11/2026   1.0      CannyIEC         Documented existing behaviour\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n================================================================================\n*)\nMETHOD cdr : CONS_REG\nVAR_INPUT\n\thead : CONS_REG;\nEND_VAR\nVAR\n\tcell : ConsCell;\nEND_VAR\n",
                  "LineInfoPersistence": "(string)fcfe7f67-243d-48af-854c-5b0df9b9c3a3_Decl_LineIds"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "TypeInfos": {
        "3b83b776": "{3b83b776-fb25-43b8-99f2-3c507c9143fc}",
